7Bob5IrziwS46VQdKtLvNC0uQfp2lugPgB3IA1o/vq8P0+g\n6oCK+JlroHLK7XRG6SoH6Vazr4buGt2bYZdOoK1ttqNDHTpEa99DTDye0NHi\ni8ZCgdljwmO71MZ23Io2UHhHpIYef++wJqPnOstNllkMc70fPkLQV7MkUUnm\nkHRhoZ0v2vRYmTz8KkXCynLBGuxexHIqJWlEGnD/6eTyfk3+mARLPRjATb1q\ncm4Odq52MGQZOWgPf4T2qa1ttH6RMPXFhraH9OZhBvOQKeExbGslEJ9XKBZp\ne/ZcpHzY4J6TR0xSeq3VWx08IECUvkGgqSKa20bLlCMAfqmAGYtiP3ZsnDuX\n0jMCJFLkYlATD0WQHBCilt0im/MMSgCsF1Z5vpLWn6yeCqckVwZWr8mXGRbs\nUSqvyRdvEOs26/rXihn1FMwhiqtdpCLg3cMZbBi+x5dGqJzteDzEF/Vk+7gE\ng4kQN+j3wSo+binPPLvoZoFWpQcpWnijDpZMjNJVaqMsS/yrIwbH5Q==\n",
    "teacher_markdown": "**Students may upload a mood board but not reference it in their prompt**\r\n\r\nSome students may attach the mood board and assume the AI will automatically know what to do with it. Encourage them to explicitly connect the image to their request by asking: \"What do you want the AI to notice about this mood board?\" Remind students that the AI works best when they explain which colors, styles, or design elements they want to use.\r\n\r\n**Students may focus only on colors and miss other design elements**\r\n\r\nStudents often notice the color palette but overlook fonts, layout, spacing, or overall mood. Help them think more broadly by asking: \"Besides colors, what design choices from the mood board stand out to you?\" Encourage students to describe the feeling or style they want the website to capture.\r\n\r\n**Students may expect the AI to perfectly match the mood board on the first try**\r\n\r\nSome students may become frustrated if the first result doesn't look exactly as expected. Remind them that design is an iterative process by asking: \"What's one specific thing you'd like the AI to improve?\" Encourage students to make small, focused requests rather than starting over completely.\r\n\r\n**Students may struggle to describe why they don't like the result**\r\n\r\nStudents may say, \"It doesn't look right,\" without being able to explain why. Help them develop design vocabulary by asking: \"What feels different from the mood board?\" or \"Is it the colors, fonts, layout, or overall mood?\" This can help them create more effective follow-up prompts."
  },
